IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa19-nouns`

-- coa19-ch1-registrar.l4: Part 25, Chapter 1 (Companies registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland), cross-headings "The register of charges",
-- "Avoidance of certain charges" and "Companies' records and registers": ss 869 to 877, lines 11932-12016 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1: the law as the text states it. A provision that addresses only the registrar is encoded for what it decides and what it gives the person.
--
-- SEAMS taken as inputs: `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` (coa23), `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24),
-- `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection` (coa25), `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` (keel),
-- `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` (keel, BOOLEAN suffices). "such fee as may be prescribed" is a plain NUMBER input.

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter 1 -- The register of charges, avoidance, records and registers (ss 869 to 877)`

§§ `s 869 Register of charges to be kept by registrar`

-- src:11934 | (1) The registrar shall keep, with respect to each company, a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter.
@ref s 869(1) The registrar shall keep, with respect to each company, a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter (src:11934-11934)
GIVEN `the charge requires registration under Chapter 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(1) the registrar must keep the charge in the register of charges` MEANS
    IF `the charge requires registration under Chapter 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register of all the charges requiring registration under this Chapter"

-- src:11935 | (2) In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled, the registrar shall enter in the register the required particulars specified in section 863(2).
@ref s 869(2) In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled, the registrar shall enter in the register the required particulars specified in section 863(2) (src:11935-11935)
GIVEN `the charge is one to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(2) the registrar must enter the required particulars specified in section 863(2)` MEANS
    IF `the charge is one to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a charge to the benefit of which holders of a series of debentures are entitled"

-- src:11936 | (3) In the case of a charge imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office under Article 46 of the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981, the registrar shall enter in the register the date on which the charge became effective.
@ref s 869(3) In the case of a charge imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office under Article 46 of the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981, the registrar shall enter in the register the date on which the charge became effective (src:11936-11936)
GIVEN `the charge is one imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office under Article 46 of the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(3) the registrar must enter the date on which the charge became effective` MEANS
    IF `the charge is one imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office under Article 46 of the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a charge imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office under Article 46 of the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981"

DECLARE `s 869(4) particular` IS ONE OF
    `s 869(4)(a) the date of its creation`
    `s 869(4)(a) the date of the acquisition`
    `s 869(4)(b) the amount secured by the charge`
    `s 869(4)(c) short particulars of the property charged`
    `s 869(4)(d) the persons entitled to the charge`
    `s 869(4) any other particular`

-- src:11937 | (4) In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars—
-- src:11938 | (a) if it is a charge created by a company, the date of its creation and, if it is a charge which was existing on property acquired by the company, the date of the acquisition,
-- src:11939 | (b) the amount secured by the charge,
-- src:11940 | (c) short particulars of the property charged, and
-- src:11941 | (d) the persons entitled to the charge.
@ref s 869(4) In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars (src:11937-11941)
GIVEN `the charge is one other than a charge of a series of debentures or a charge imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is a charge created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is one which was existing on property acquired by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      particular IS A `s 869(4) particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(4) the registrar must enter the particular in the register` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the charge is one other than a charge of a series of debentures or a charge imposed by the Enforcement of Judgments Office`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of any other charge, the registrar shall enter in the register the following particulars—"
        IF particular EQUALS `s 869(4) any other particular` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following particulars—"
        IF particular EQUALS `s 869(4)(a) the date of its creation` THEN (IF `the charge is a charge created by a company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        IF particular EQUALS `s 869(4)(a) the date of the acquisition` THEN (IF `the charge is one which was existing on property acquired by the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11942 | (5) The registrar shall give a certificate of the registration of any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter, stating the amount secured by the charge.
@ref s 869(5) The registrar shall give a certificate of the registration of any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter, stating the amount secured by the charge (src:11942-11942)
GIVEN `the charge is registered in pursuance of Chapter 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(5) the registrar must give a certificate of the registration of the charge, stating the amount secured by the charge` MEANS
    IF `the charge is registered in pursuance of Chapter 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter": the duty is to certify a charge registered in pursuance of this Chapter; the text says nothing of any other charge

-- src:11943 | (6) The certificate—
-- src:11944 | (a) shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal, and
@ref s 869(6)(a) The certificate shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal (src:11943-11944)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(6)(a) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is signed by the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1062 the document bears the registrar's official seal`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be signed by the registrar or authenticated by the registrar's official seal"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the certificate bears the official seal is s 1062, which another part answers

-- src:11945 | (b) is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Chapter as to registration have been satisfied.
@ref s 869(6)(b) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Chapter as to registration have been satisfied (src:11945-11945)
GIVEN `a certificate of the registration of the charge has been given under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(6)(b) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of Chapter 1 as to registration have been satisfied` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of the registration of the charge has been given under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no certificate has been given

-- src:11946 | (7) The register kept in pursuance of this section shall be open to inspection by any person.
@ref s 869(7) The register kept in pursuance of this section shall be open to inspection by any person (src:11946-11946)
GIVEN `the register is the register kept by the registrar in pursuance of section 869` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 869(7) the register is open to inspection by any person` MEANS
    IF `the register is the register kept by the registrar in pursuance of section 869`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The register kept in pursuance of this section"

§§ `s 870 The period allowed for registration`

-- src:11948 | (1) The period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company is—
-- src:11949 | (a) 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the charge is created, or
-- src:11950 | (b) if the charge is created outside the United Kingdom, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 870(1) The period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company (src:11948-11950)
GIVEN `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the charge is created` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 870(1) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge created by a company` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the charge is created`

-- src:11951 | (2) The period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject is—
-- src:11952 | (a) 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the acquisition is completed, or
-- src:11953 | (b) if the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 870(2) The period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject (src:11951-11953)
GIVEN `the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the acquisition is completed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 870(2) the last day of the period allowed for registration of a charge to which property acquired by a company is subject` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated and the charge was created outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced (or a copy of it) could, in due course of post (and if despatched with due diligence) have been received in the United Kingdom`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the acquisition is completed`

-- src:11954 | (3) The period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures as a result of section 863 is—
-- src:11955 | (a) if there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 863(1), 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which that deed is executed, or
-- src:11956 | (b) if there is no such deed, 21 days beginning with the day after the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed.
@ref s 870(3) The period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures as a result of section 863 (src:11954-11956)
GIVEN `there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 863(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that deed is executed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 870(3) the last day of the period allowed for registration of particulars of a series of debentures` MEANS
    IF `there is a deed containing the charge mentioned in section 863(1)`
    THEN `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which that deed is executed`
    ELSE `s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` `the day on which the first debenture of the series is executed`

§§ `s 871 Registration of enforcement of security`

-- src:11958 | (1) If a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property, or appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument, he shall within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers, give notice of the fact to the registrar.
@ref s 871(1) If a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property, or appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument, he shall within 7 days give notice of the fact to the registrar (src:11958-11958)
GIVEN `a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` MEANS
    IF `a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property` OR `a person appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property, or appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument"

-- src:11958 | (1) If a person obtains an order for the appointment of a receiver or manager of a company's property, or appoints such a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument, he shall within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers, give notice of the fact to the registrar.
@ref s 871(1) within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers (src:11958-11958)
GIVEN `the day of the order or of the appointment under those powers` IS A DATE
      `the day the person gave the registrar notice of the fact` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 871(1) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` MEANS
    `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` `the day the person gave the registrar notice of the fact` (`s 859K(2) the last day of 7 days after` `the day of the order or of the appointment under those powers`) `the day the question is asked`

-- src:11959 | (2) Where a person appointed receiver or manager of a company's property under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act as such receiver or manager, he shall, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect.
@ref s 871(2) Where a person appointed receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act, he shall, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect (src:11959-11959)
GIVEN `a person appointed receiver or manager of a company's property under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act as such receiver or manager` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 871(2) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect` MEANS
    IF `a person appointed receiver or manager of a company's property under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act as such receiver or manager`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person appointed receiver or manager of a company's property under powers contained in an instrument ceases to act as such receiver or manager"

-- src:11960 | (3) The registrar must enter a fact of which he is given notice under this section in the register of charges.
@ref s 871(3) The registrar must enter a fact of which he is given notice under this section in the register of charges (src:11960-11960)
GIVEN `the registrar is given notice of a fact under section 871` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 871(3) the registrar must enter the fact in the register of charges` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is given notice of a fact under section 871`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection is about a fact of which notice has been given

-- src:11961 | (4) A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of this section commits an offence.
@ref s 871(4) A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of this section commits an offence (src:11961-11961)
GIVEN `s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 871(2) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person made default in complying with the requirements of section 871` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 871(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 871(2) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of this section commits an offence": no requirement of the section binds the person
        IF (`s 871(1) the person must give notice of the fact to the registrar within 7 days` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 871(2) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice to that effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN (IF `the person made default in complying with the requirements of section 871` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who makes default in complying with the requirements of this section commits an offence": JUST FALSE where there is no default
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:11962 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 871(5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale (src:11962-11962)
`s 871(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

§§ `s 872 Entries of satisfaction and release`

-- src:11964 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to a registered charge—
-- src:11965 | (a) that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part, or
-- src:11966 | (b) that part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking.
@ref s 872(1) Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to a registered charge that the debt has been paid or satisfied, or that part of the property has been released (src:11964-11966)
GIVEN `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 872(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` OR `a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying that part of the property or undertaking charged has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies if a statement is delivered to the registrar verifying with respect to a registered charge—"

-- src:11967 | (2) The registrar may enter on the register a memorandum of satisfaction in whole or in part, or of the fact part of the property or undertaking has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking (as the case may be).
@ref s 872(2) The registrar may enter on the register a memorandum of satisfaction in whole or in part (src:11967-11967)
GIVEN `s 872(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 872(2) the registrar may enter a memorandum of satisfaction or of release on the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 872(1) subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies if": the power is given on that gate and the text does not say it has none otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:11968 | (3) Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, the registrar shall if required send the company a copy of it.
@ref s 872(3) Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, the registrar shall if required send the company a copy of it (src:11968-11968)
GIVEN `the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company requires a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 872(3) the registrar must send the company a copy of the memorandum` MEANS
    IF `the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole` AND `the company requires a copy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the registrar enters a memorandum of satisfaction in whole, the registrar shall if required send the company a copy of it"

§§ `s 873 Rectification of register of charges`

-- src:11970 | (1) Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—
-- src:11971 | (a) that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of any particular with respect to any such charge or in a memorandum of satisfaction—
-- src:11972 | (i) was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause, or
-- src:11973 | (ii) is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company, or
-- src:11974 | (b) that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief.
@ref s 873(1) Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied (src:11970-11974)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of a particular, was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the failure, omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 873(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF       `the court is satisfied that the failure to register a charge before the end of the period allowed for registration, or the omission or mis-statement of a particular, was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that the failure, omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders of the company`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—"

DECLARE `s 873(2) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 873(2) an order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended`
    `s 873(2) an order that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified`
    `s 873(2) any other order`

-- src:11975 | (2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, and on such terms and conditions as seem to the court just and expedient, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified.
@ref s 873(2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified (src:11975-11975)
GIVEN `s 873(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the company or a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 873(2) order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 873(2) the court may make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 873(1) subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (2) applies if the court is satisfied—": the power is given on that gate and the text does not say it has none otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the application is made by the company or a person interested`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of the company or a person interested"
            IF order EQUALS `s 873(2) any other order`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11975 | (2) The court may, on the application of the company or a person interested, and on such terms and conditions as seem to the court just and expedient, order that the period allowed for registration shall be extended or, as the case may be, that the omission or mis-statement shall be rectified.
@ref s 873(2) the period allowed for registration shall be extended (src:11975-11975)
GIVEN `the last day of the period allowed for registration` IS A DATE
      `the last day to which an order under subsection (2) extends the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 873(2) the last day of the period allowed for registration as extended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day to which an order under subsection (2) extends the period`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN lastDay
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of the period allowed for registration`

§§ `s 874 Consequence of failure to register charges created by a company`

DECLARE `s 874(1) party against whom the charge may be void` IS ONE OF
    `s 874(1)(a) a liquidator of the company`
    `s 874(1)(b) an administrator of the company`
    `s 874(1)(c) a creditor of the company`
    `s 874(1) any other person`

-- src:11978 | (1) If a company creates a charge to which section 860 applies, the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against—
-- src:11979 | (a) a liquidator of the company,
-- src:11980 | (b) an administrator of the company, and
-- src:11981 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:11982 | unless that section is complied with.
@ref s 874(1) If a company creates a charge to which section 860 applies, the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against a liquidator, an administrator and a creditor unless that section is complied with (src:11978-11982)
GIVEN `a company creates a charge to which section 860 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 860 is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      party IS A `s 874(1) party against whom the charge may be void`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 874(1) the charge is void against the party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a company creates a charge to which section 860 applies`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company creates a charge to which section 860 applies"
        IF `section 860 is complied with`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that section is complied with"
        IF party EQUALS `s 874(1) any other person`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the charge is void (so far as any security on the company's property or undertaking is conferred by it) against—"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11983 | (2) Subsection (1) is subject to the provisions of this Chapter.
@ref s 874(2) Subsection (1) is subject to the provisions of this Chapter (src:11983-11983)
GIVEN `s 874(1) the charge is void against the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `another provision of Chapter 1 applies to the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 874(2) the charge is void against the party, subject to the provisions of Chapter 1` MEANS
    IF `another provision of Chapter 1 applies to the charge`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) is subject to the provisions of this Chapter": the effect of the other provision is for that provision to say
    ELSE `s 874(1) the charge is void against the party`

-- src:11984 | (3) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 874(3) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge (src:11984-11984)
GIVEN `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 874(3) subsection (1) prejudices the contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` MEANS
    IF `there is a contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is nothing for subsection (1) to prejudice

-- src:11984 | (3) Subsection (1) is without prejudice to any contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge; and when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable.
@ref s 874(3) when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable (src:11984-11984)
GIVEN `s 874(1) the charge is void against the party` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 874(3) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 874(1) the charge is void against the party`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a charge becomes void under this section, the money secured by it immediately becomes payable": "when" counts as "where"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

§§ `s 875 Companies to keep copies of instruments creating charges`

-- src:11987 | (1) A company must keep available for inspection a copy of every instrument creating a charge requiring registration under this Chapter, including any document delivered to the company under section 868(3)(b) (Northern Ireland: orders imposing charges affecting land).
@ref s 875(1) A company must keep available for inspection a copy of every instrument creating a charge requiring registration under this Chapter, including any document delivered to the company under section 868(3)(b) (src:11987-11987)
GIVEN `the instrument creates a charge requiring registration under Chapter 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was delivered to the company under section 868(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 875(1) the company must keep a copy of the instrument available for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the instrument creates a charge requiring registration under Chapter 1` OR `the document was delivered to the company under section 868(3)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including any document delivered to the company under section 868(3)(b)"

-- src:11988 | (2) In the case of a series of uniform debentures, a copy of one of the debentures of the series is sufficient.
@ref s 875(2) In the case of a series of uniform debentures, a copy of one of the debentures of the series is sufficient (src:11988-11988)
GIVEN `the instruments are a series of uniform debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a copy of one of the debentures of the series` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 875(2) a copy of one of the debentures is sufficient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the instruments are a series of uniform debentures`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a series of uniform debentures"
        IF `the company keeps a copy of one of the debentures of the series` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what is sufficient, not what is insufficient

§§ `s 876 Company's register of charges`

DECLARE `s 876(1) kind of charge` IS ONE OF
    `s 876(1)(a) a charge specifically affecting property of the company`
    `s 876(1)(b) a floating charge on the whole or part of the company's property or undertaking`
    `s 876(1) any other charge`

-- src:11990 | (1) Every limited company shall keep available for inspection a register of charges and enter in it—
-- src:11991 | (a) all charges specifically affecting property of the company, and
-- src:11992 | (b) all floating charges on the whole or part of the company's property or undertaking.
@ref s 876(1) Every limited company shall keep available for inspection a register of charges and enter in it (src:11990-11992)
GIVEN `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 876(1) kind of charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 876(1) the company must enter the charge in its register of charges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `s 3(1) the company is a limited company`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every limited company shall keep available for inspection a register of charges": the duty is laid on limited companies and the text says nothing of any other company
        IF kind EQUALS `s 876(1) any other charge`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "enter in it—"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 876(2) item of the entry` IS ONE OF
    `s 876(2) a short description of the property charged`
    `s 876(2) the amount of the charge`
    `s 876(2) the names of the persons entitled to it`
    `s 876(2) any other item`

-- src:11993 | (2) The entry shall in each case give a short description of the property charged, the amount of the charge and, except in the cases of securities to bearer, the names of the persons entitled to it.
@ref s 876(2) The entry shall in each case give a short description of the property charged, the amount of the charge and, except in the cases of securities to bearer, the names of the persons entitled to it (src:11993-11993)
GIVEN item IS A `s 876(2) item of the entry`
      `the charge is a security to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 876(2) the entry must give the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item EQUALS `s 876(2) any other item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The entry shall in each case give"
        IF item EQUALS `s 876(2) the names of the persons entitled to it` AND `the charge is a security to bearer`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in the cases of securities to bearer"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11994 | (3) If an officer of the company knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of this section, he commits an offence.
@ref s 876(3) If an officer of the company knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of this section, he commits an offence (src:11994-11994)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of section 876` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 876(3) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of section 876`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an officer of the company knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the omission of an entry required to be made in pursuance of this section"
    ELSE `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`

-- src:11995 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:11996 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:11997 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 876(4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on conviction on indictment to a fine, on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (src:11995-11997)
`s 876(4) the penalties for the offence` MEANS
    LIST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
         , (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

§§ `s 877 Instruments creating charges and register of charges to be available for inspection`

-- src:11999 | (1) This section applies to—
-- src:12000 | (a) documents required to be kept available for inspection under section 875 (copies of instruments creating charges), and
-- src:12001 | (b) a company's register of charges kept in pursuance of section 876.
@ref s 877(1) This section applies to the documents required to be kept under section 875 and to a company's register of charges kept under section 876 (src:11999-12001)
GIVEN `the documents are required to be kept available for inspection under section 875, or are a company's register of charges kept in pursuance of section 876` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 877(1) this section applies to the documents and register` MEANS
    IF `the documents are required to be kept available for inspection under section 875, or are a company's register of charges kept in pursuance of section 876`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to—": a scope list with no "only" (as in s 860(7), fork F-C2)

-- src:12002 | (2) The documents and register must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:12003 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:12004 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 877(2) The documents and register must be kept available for inspection at the company's registered office or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (src:12002-12004)
GIVEN `the documents and register are kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 877(2) the documents and register are kept at a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the documents and register are kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1136 Regulations about where certain company records to be kept available for inspection`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The documents and register must be kept available for inspection—": a bare "must", not met (fork F-P1 in NOTES.md)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the places specified in regulations under s 1136 are another section's answer

-- src:12005 | (3) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:12006 | (a) of the place at which the documents and register are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:12007 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:12008 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 877(3) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place, unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office (src:12005-12008)
GIVEN `the documents and register have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 877(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place` MEANS
    IF `the documents and register have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 877(4) terms of inspection` IS ONE OF
    `s 877(4)(a) open to inspection without charge`
    `s 877(4)(b) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` HAS `the fee in pounds that is prescribed` IS A NUMBER

-- src:12009 | (4) The documents and register shall be open to the inspection—
-- src:12010 | (a) of any creditor or member of the company without charge, and
-- src:12011 | (b) of any other person on payment of such fee as may be prescribed.
@ref s 877(4) The documents and register shall be open to the inspection of any creditor or member of the company without charge, and of any other person on payment of such fee as may be prescribed (src:12009-12011)
GIVEN `the person is a creditor or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee prescribed for any other person, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 877(4) terms of inspection`
`s 877(4) the terms on which the documents and register must be open to the inspection of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a creditor or member of the company`
    THEN `s 877(4)(a) open to inspection without charge`
    ELSE `s 877(4)(b) open to inspection on payment of the prescribed fee` `the fee prescribed for any other person, in pounds`

-- src:12012 | (5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—
@ref s 877(5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed (src:12012-12012)
GIVEN `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 877(5) an offence is committed` MEANS
    IF `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` AT LEAST 14 OR `an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3) or an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—"

-- src:12013 | (a) the company, and
