      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 877(5)(b) the officer commits the offence` MEANS
    `s 859A both answers hold` (`the offence is committed under subsection (5)`) (`s 859A both answers hold` `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

-- src:12015 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 877(6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale (src:12015-12015)
`s 877(6) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE

-- src:12016 | (7) If an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused the court may by order compel an immediate inspection.
@ref s 877(7) If an inspection required under subsection (4) is refused the court may by order compel an immediate inspection (src:12016-12016)
